d8527e92df75050deeb16e270bb18170d83dd172b8bc2621e5","event_uuid":"6b08170d-6328-4917-ab88-faee04e03cd9","position":{"commit_sha":"7dbbb184f79628125427b964a3a46bee797bf861","position":"1793796062773041001-6b08170d-6328-4917-ab88-faee04e03cd9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause: 463739cdb48 (2026-07-03) added the first-run seed from /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref with only a resolvability check. Nothing in the repo or on the host writes the marker (host grep: only autodeploy.sh references it); rsync excludes it. Host read-only 2026-11-04: deployed-sha = mcp-deployed-sha = bot-deployed-sha = 4496e9acd2a; marker d4a0a2a44 resolves in the mirror but merge-base --is-ancestor origin/main rc=1. Fix pushed as Gerrit 3298: seed only from a main ancestor, else adopt the tip and emit AUTODEPLOY_ERROR deployed-ref-off-main. Tests: tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_first_run_seed.py, off-main case failed before the fix (seeded the side commit) and passes after; 156/156 autodeploy tests, make lint, make typecheck green.\n\nOPERATOR STEP (not performed; production is read-only for agents): remove the stale marker on i-00880b2c7f13527c5 so the next state loss cannot even raise the deployed-ref-off-main signal:\n  sudo rm /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref\nSafe on the current host: steady state never reads it (deployed-sha is populated), and the fixed script refuses it anyway.","timestamp":1793791786760364001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3298 merged as fe6c2100292 (patch set 2; PS1 Verified -1 was tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py flagging a raw os.environ copy in the new test, fixed by using subprocess_env). Deployed by autodeploy's own MCP-delta path (autodeploy.sh is in MCP_PATHS): rsync from mirror, self re-exec, blue-green MCP roll; deploy complete 2026-11-04 04:30 PST, host deployed-sha = mcp = bot = fe6c2100292, installed script contains deployed-ref-off-main. Left in_progress: the operator step (sudo rm /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref on i-00880b2c7f13527c5) remains.","timestamp":1793795519731145001}],"created_at":1793754096639944001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9dad1a06-55e8-44bf-be57-f1e228e8e56f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"007c-dabe-21a5-4e92"},{"link_uuid":"818be608-148b-4bce-a058-1fbf85a2a73e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"024f-7424-2183-4b73"},{"link_uuid":"7cf641e2-166c-4fd5-a4a4-3cabb94a5bb8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0ded-ffcd-e4e2-484a"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n/opt/rebar/.deployed_ref on rebar-gerrit (i-00880b2c7f13527c5) reads \"d4a0a2a44 (feat/gerrit-ci-verified-gate)\", mtime 2026-07-02 18:17 UTC. That commit is NOT an ancestor of origin/main (`git merge-base --is-ancestor` rc=1 in the host mirror, checked read-only 2026-11-04), but the host mirror /var/lib/rebar/mirror still resolves it.\n\nThe only reader is infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh's first-run seed (the `if [ -z \"$DEPLOYED\" ]` block after the fetch). It runs only when /var/lib/rebar/deployed-sha is empty. Today deployed-sha, mcp-deployed-sha and bot-deployed-sha all hold 4496e9acd2a (= origin/main), so steady state never reads the marker. If deployed-sha is lost (state wipe, re-provision of /var/lib/rebar), autodeploy adopts the July feature-branch commit as \"deployed\", and the next tick computes every component delta from d4a0a2a44..main.\n\nRoot cause: commit 463739cdb48 (2026-07-03, ADR 0079 box-adapt) added the seed so the first autodeploy run would record what the pre-autodeploy hand copy-deploy had installed. It accepts any ref the mirror can resolve and never checks that the ref is on main. Nothing in the repo or on the host writes the marker any more (host grep across /etc, /usr/local, cron, /root, /home and /opt/rebar finds only autodeploy.sh), and rsync excludes it, so the marker can only go staler.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep the seed's original intent (adopt a hand-deploy record that is a real main commit) and add the guard it lacked. Accept the marker only when it resolves to a commit AND `git merge-base --is-ancestor <ref> $TARGET` succeeds. Otherwise fall back to the existing default (adopt $TARGET, no deploy) and emit `err deployed-ref-off-main` naming the rejected ref, so an operator learns that the marker is stale and should be removed. This mirrors the script's existing pattern for invalid component markers (fall back to a known-good value) and its convention of announcing a rejected input with an AUTODEPLOY_ERROR marker.\n\nHealthy-host behaviour is unchanged: the block only runs when deployed-sha is empty. No compose files, logging, or the MCP deploy path are touched.\n\n## Scope\n\n- infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh: the first-run seed block only.\n- tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_first_run_seed.py (new): drives the real script against a throwaway real git mirror; a `git` wrapper intercepts only `remote get-url` and `fetch` and passes everything else to real git.\n\nOut of scope: removing /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref on the host. That is an operator step, recorded on this ticket.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew tests, all with an empty deployed-sha:\n- marker = an ancestor of main -> deployed-sha = that commit (intent preserved, already passes).\n- marker = an off-main commit the mirror resolves -> deployed-sha = TARGET, and an AUTODEPLOY_ERROR with reason deployed-ref-off-main naming the ref (fails before the fix).\n- marker unresolvable -> deployed-sha = TARGET (existing behaviour).\n- no marker -> deployed-sha = TARGET (existing behaviour).\n- deployed-sha already set -> the marker is ignored and deployed-sha is untouched.\nThen the existing tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_*.py suite, `make lint` (includes shellcheck) and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] With an empty deployed-sha and an off-main .deployed_ref, autodeploy seeds deployed-sha to origin/main and emits AUTODEPLOY_ERROR reason=deployed-ref-off-main; a test pins this.\n- [x] With an empty deployed-sha and a main-ancestor .deployed_ref, autodeploy still seeds from the marker; a test pins this.\n- [x] Missing or unresolvable markers still seed origin/main; tests pin both.\n- [x] tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_*.py, `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass in the worktree.\n- [x] The change merges through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The host operator step (remove the stale /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref on i-00880b2c7f13527c5) is recorded on this ticket as a comment with the exact command.\n  provenance: environment=rebar tracker (tickets branch on origin); principal=Rebar Bot Nava via worktree .venv/bin/rebar; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the comment carrying `sudo rm /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref` was written with `rebar comment` on 2026-11-04 and is on this ticket; the removal itself is NOT performed and remains with the host operator.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"guard the first-run .deployed_ref seed with a main-ancestry check"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_first_run_seed.py","reason":"pin first-run seed behaviour on an empty deployed-sha"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","024f-7424-2183-4b73"],["relates_to","0ded-ffcd-e4e2-484a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"75aaf600-42df-4ef3-8c0a-2801861699f9","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":4,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ops-sweep"],"ticket_id":"b5b8-0194-c1eb-49ba","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Stale /opt/rebar/.deployed_ref would seed autodeploy off-main","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["02d24737-a9c1-459a-b650-8722f3f9d882","5978c239-c866-4da1-a5c1-6f398ff64e14","b7f28ff9-b8e8-437b-88aa-6315bb7155fc","75aaf600-42df-4ef3-8c0a-2801861699f9","98af9a98-ae2c-4c60-b778-47ace04d0c3b","f2485a02-cbfc-4edf-b18d-cc1a1fc9765f","818be608-148b-4bce-a058-1fbf85a2a73e","7cf641e2-166c-4fd5-a4a4-3cabb94a5bb8","5b72e965-7fbf-47c4-bb6a-3d18a916a302","9361dfed-3394-4d37-a7d0-3a069111c425","6b08170d-6328-4917-ab88-faee04e03cd9"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793796062773041002,"uuid":"28fd18e3-eeef-4c72-8ee4-b51e6d68f1b8"}